WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.130
Joe: A Brit and an American swap countries

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.990
to try each other's McDonald's.

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.457
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.600
We'll start with some things
you can find in the UK

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.500
but I think might be
slightly different over here.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.740
Let's start with the
iconic McDonald's Big Mac.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.190
So, I mean, visually,
looks pretty much the same.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.530
You've got the quite
sad, flimsy beef patties.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.789
Let's give it a try.

00:00:22.318 --> 00:00:24.023
So, I think there are some
subtle differences there,

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:25.920
actually. Like, broadly speaking,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.440
if you gave it to me and were
like, "This is a UK Big Mac,"

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.480
I don't think I would doubt you.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.363
I think it's the sauce,
because the UK Big Mac sauce

00:00:33.363 --> 00:00:37.470
has got quite a tang to it,
almost, and this is very gentle.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.700
I barely get anything from it.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.760
The Big Mac. Now, this
looks exactly like a Big Mac

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.930
anywhere in the world.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.463
You know what I gotta do. Oop and oop.

00:00:45.463 --> 00:00:46.813
Now let's give this a shot.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.320
If that isn't exactly
the same, it's close.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.140
I mean, if I could do one side
by side I'd probably notice,

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.082
but I do not taste any difference.

00:00:55.082 --> 00:00:57.120
I remember when we did
"Fast-Food Chemistry,"

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.100
you guys had more
chemicals and stuff to use,

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.240
but I'm here to say

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.370
the chemicals have not
made a striking difference.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.080
It tastes almost exactly the same.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.630
Then we're on to the fries and
the Coke aspect of the meal.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.270
Firstly, I have to point
out how enormous these are.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.920
The size of this drink is ridiculous.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:11.753
This is way bigger

00:01:11.753 --> 00:01:14.700
than almost any fast-food
drink I've seen in the UK ever.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.250
Even the fries as well.
This box of fries is huge.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.600
They've kind of sunk down a little bit,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.940
so it doesn't really show how full it was.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.740
But this carton is massive.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.420
You can fit so many fries in here.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.410
It feels like almost double the size

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.020
of a carton of UK fries.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.400
I mean, these are pretty good.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.710
I will say, I think they've
held up a lot better

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:33.270
after a bit of time out of the fryer

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.350
than UK fries have.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.150
UK McDonald's fries, I think maybe

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.980
because they don't have
as many ingredients,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.001
there aren't the preservative
chemicals in there,

00:01:40.001 --> 00:01:41.550
they don't really hold
up very well at all.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.480
As soon as they come out the fryer,

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.190
they kind of just get
worse and worse and worse.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.200
So you have to eat them
really while they're hot.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.580
I think taste-wise,

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.500
there are some slight differences as well.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.730
There is something more than
just salt going on here.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:54.957
So, I only know this because we made

00:01:54.957 --> 00:01:58.350
that "Fast-Food Chemistry"
episode of McDonald's fries,

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.680
but there is a sort of
artificial-beef flavor

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.500
that's added to these, and
you do kind of taste it.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.540
It's very subtle, but there's a kind of

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.000
savory depth of flavor to these

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.460
that you just don't get in the UK.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.380
I kind of like it. I can't lie.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:14.760
My first thing about these fries,

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:17.460
these guys are pale looking.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.710
Not the bright yellow I'm
used to in the States.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:22.743
The whole thing is just potato,
salt, and oil, that's it?

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:29.493
Yeah, and I believe it,
because these are bland.

00:02:29.493 --> 00:02:30.665
Man!

00:02:30.665 --> 00:02:31.498
What?

00:02:31.498 --> 00:02:35.289
Mm-mm, no on the fries.
USA ones are way better.

00:02:35.289 --> 00:02:37.780
And then finally, this
enormous McDonald's Coke.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.920
I don't know what it is
about McDonald's Coke,

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.270
but it just always hits different.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:43.560
That happens in the UK

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.330
and, yeah, kind of still happens here.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.346
Another iconic menu item

00:02:46.346 --> 00:02:48.930
that I thought was worth
trying was McNuggets.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.060
So, just visually speaking,
before I even try it,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.460
these look quite different
to British McNuggets.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.100
I'm fairly sure the ones
in the UK are deep-fried.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.900
Correct me if I'm wrong, editor.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.698
But these ones look almost
more deep-fried somehow,

00:03:01.698 --> 00:03:04.062
just in terms of the way that the breading

00:03:04.062 --> 00:03:06.480
has kind of puffed up and
blistered a little bit.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.313
I will say, I think the breading

00:03:07.313 --> 00:03:09.210
maybe has slightly more seasoning,

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.430
a bit more flavor going
on here than I'm used to.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.890
The chicken itself I think
is pretty much the same.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.260
I think I might prefer
British nuggets. Sorry, guys.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.350
Nuggets look like almost
exactly the same size,

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:23.100
smell the same, same amount
of crispness on the skin.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:27.900
No, much blander. Much blander.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.910
You guys are getting a terrible deal

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.093
with these nuggets, because this is dry.

00:03:32.093 --> 00:03:33.950
I did notice it says
"100% chicken breast meat"

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.190
on this one.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.750
I do not know if that's
the case in America.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.610
Can we get that on-screen?

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.960
But I've just been informed, no,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.360
of the chicken that they use,

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.970
100% of it is chicken breast meat,

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.520
but it's only 45% chicken, right?

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.920
It says "100% chicken breast" on it.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.830
The implication there is that
the chicken is 100% chicken,

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.080
or it's 100% chicken meat.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:57.180
It is not. Deceptive!

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:58.200
The last thing we wanted to compare

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.990
in both countries was the McCrispy.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:02.850
Here is an American McCrispy.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:05.850
It looks fairly similar
to ours on the surface.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.862
This one I think is a
potato roll rather than

00:04:08.862 --> 00:04:11.007
the more pretzel-y brioche version

00:04:11.007 --> 00:04:12.090
that you find in the UK.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:13.770
There's no sauce.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.770
It's just pickles and
a fried chicken patty.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.970
I really like the pickles.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:20.970
I think pickles and fried
chicken is a great combination,

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.860
and it's not super common in the UK.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.270
I will say, I think it needs a sauce.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:27.090
I think technically they claim
that they butter the rolls

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.970
and that butter is I
guess therefore the sauce,

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.560
but it's kind of dry.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.330
The chicken's just a
little bit thin as well.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.053
I feel like the McCrispy
in the UK tends to be

00:04:35.053 --> 00:04:37.860
a thicker and slightly
juicier piece of chicken.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:42.180
This is a fairly thin and
quite dry chicken breast.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.503
The McCrispy.

00:04:43.503 --> 00:04:44.340
Harry: Yellow box.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.620
Oh, nice! All right.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.720
I'm pleasantly surprised by the bun.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.000
It reminds me of King's Hawaiian rolls.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.580
Yeah, this looks like our McChicken.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.420
It is so close to the McChicken.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:57.095
Better bun than the McChicken,

00:04:57.095 --> 00:04:58.661
but the crispiness of the chicken patty.

00:04:58.661 --> 00:04:59.640
It tastes slightly different.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.260
I would say the McChicken sauce is,

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.300
I hate to say it, is a bit sweeter.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.258
Because I love the McChicken.

00:05:04.258 --> 00:05:06.133
Like, the taste of that is in my DNA.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.700
Here are all the US menu items

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.610
you won't find at a UK McDonald's.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.658
Here's all the UK McDonald's menu items

00:05:13.658 --> 00:05:15.270
I can't get in the US.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:16.680
We'll start with some chicken options,

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.621
namely the deluxe McCrispy

00:05:19.621 --> 00:05:21.721
and the spicy deluxe McCrispy.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.910
Let's take a look at the deluxe McCrispy

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.670
and see what exactly they're
adding to make it deluxe.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.580
The roll looks pretty much the
same as the standard version.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.230
The chicken looks the same.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.080
But I think when they say deluxe,

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:36.510
that just means they've added
mayo, lettuce, and tomato.

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:38.160
I don't know if that is enough

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.840
to qualify something as deluxe.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.550
Doesn't seem super deluxe to me.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:44.730
I also think that tomato is
just a bad topping for a burger.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.740
They've kind of made this
worse, in my opinion.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.458
I'm going to take a bite
of the spicy one and see

00:05:48.458 --> 00:05:50.010
if it's good and if it's spicy.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:52.410
It does have some heat to
it. They weren't kidding.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.170
For my measly British-person palate.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:57.752
I think I would probably
just buy the regular version

00:05:57.752 --> 00:06:00.660
of the McCrispy and then
add some sauce to it.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.140
So, you got a bacon mayo
chicken and a mayo chicken.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:07.380
No, this might be exactly
what the McChicken's like.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.240
Nah, it's a little wimpier.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.490
Yeah. Is this what you're talking about?

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:14.396
Like, it's a big McNugget? Yeah.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.380
The mayo's weird. Has a
really stale aftertaste.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:22.290
I'm telling you, your guys'
breaded chicken at McDonald's

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:24.515
has no flavor compared
to the one in the US.

00:06:24.515 --> 00:06:27.840
The McCrispy was crispier,
had more flavor in the sauce,

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.100
and the bun was nicer.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.203
Yeah, this is a bummer.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.480
Ugh, we got the same with
bacon. Do I really have to ...

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.688
No.

00:06:35.688 --> 00:06:38.820
Look at how flimsy your bacon is.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.200
Now we're on to some beef options,

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.150
starting with the McDouble.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:44.430
I have just some kind
of existential questions

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.496
about the McDouble.

00:06:45.496 --> 00:06:47.790
Namely, why does it exist?

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:49.206
Because we have the double cheeseburger.

00:06:49.206 --> 00:06:50.497
Let's give it try.

00:06:50.497 --> 00:06:53.280
I'm genuinely curious,
like, how is this different

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.950
to just a double cheeseburger, Joe?

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.600
One slice of cheese. Joe
says one slice of cheese.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.433
Talk me through it.

00:06:58.433 --> 00:07:00.812
OK, so what's going on
here is that the McDouble

00:07:00.812 --> 00:07:02.430
has one slice of cheese in between,

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.675
where with double cheese, we
have two slices of cheese.

00:07:04.675 --> 00:07:05.724
I think that's the only difference.

00:07:05.724 --> 00:07:06.990
I honestly think it's, right,

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.097
because this is just, like,
the standard McDonald's.

00:07:09.097 --> 00:07:09.930
Yeah, this looks very normal.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.746
Right? It's just one less slice of cheese

00:07:11.746 --> 00:07:13.925
from what we can tell. And
the price difference is,

00:07:13.925 --> 00:07:15.780
let's get that on-screen.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.360
So if you want to save
that amount of money,

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.493
get yourself a McDouble

00:07:20.493 --> 00:07:23.409
and pass the savings on to you.

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:25.680
There you go. Cheers, Joe.
You heard it here first.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:28.350
Next up we have the Quarter
Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:31.710
So, similarly to the McCrispy,

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:34.008
they've turned this thing
into a deluxe burger

00:07:34.008 --> 00:07:38.430
by just adding some lettuce,
some mayo, and some tomato.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:39.510
You know what they've tried to do here?

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:41.280
They've tried to just make a Whopper.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.580
This is the double Quarter
Pounder with bacon.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.460
Now this is a burger.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:50.160
This one does what you would
expect a Quarter Pounder to do.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.170
It's just loads of meat and cheese.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.730
I want to talk more
about this bacon as well,

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:54.840
because this bacon's good.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.910
One thing that I think we
do quite badly in the UK

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.710
at fast food is bacon.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.760
A lot of the bacon you'll
find on UK restaurants

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:04.320
is this very pallid pink color,

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:06.510
whereas this one, stronger flavor,

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.010
you get some smokiness from it.

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:09.751
The bacon on this is way better,

00:08:09.751 --> 00:08:12.360
and therefore that makes
it a very enjoyable burger.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:14.940
Yes, I think the deluxe
should just be more beef

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:17.040
and some bacon rather than vegetables

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:18.348
that no one wants to eat. Come on.

00:08:19.345 --> 00:08:21.600
Oh, yeah, now we're talking. Two patties.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.850
Although, I'm telling you
guys, the patty on patty

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.650
with nothing in the middle is just weird.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.983
A poppy-sesame-seed-bun hybrid?

00:08:28.983 --> 00:08:31.149
Whoa!

00:08:31.149 --> 00:08:32.970
Yeah, it doesn't look like barbecue sauce.

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.145
Barbecue sauce is, like, an amber brown.

00:08:35.145 --> 00:08:36.295
Eh.

00:08:36.295 --> 00:08:38.370
I think the bacon kind of screws it up

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.260
because your bacon is so flimsy.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:42.210
I think this would work
with American bacon,

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:45.175
because American bacon would
just be, like, crisp —

00:08:45.175 --> 00:08:46.675
I mean, it's not like
it has to be crispier.

00:08:46.675 --> 00:08:49.890
It's just, this is really rubbery.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:52.650
What do you guys think barbecue sauce is?

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:53.970
Bacon double cheeseburger.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.619
I'm not impressed with
your bacon here, guys.

00:08:55.619 --> 00:08:56.594
I'm not impressed.

00:08:56.594 --> 00:08:59.394
Look. Look at ...

00:08:59.394 --> 00:09:01.504
everyone in America,
look how weird this is.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:04.037
Yeah, like ...

00:09:05.012 --> 00:09:06.513
I'm pretty sure we had a
bacon double cheeseburger

00:09:06.513 --> 00:09:08.760
at some point at McDonald's,
and it wasn't like this.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:12.665
Our bacon is crispier, more
dispersed evenly, I guess.

00:09:12.665 --> 00:09:14.970
Just have two strips going
right through the middle here.

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:17.580
That's a disaster. It's a total disaster!

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.410
All right, McPlant. Harry, get in here

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.480
and explain to me what
I'm doing, what this is.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.210
This is the McPlant. It's
McDonald's fake-meat burger.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:25.920
It took them ages to develop this.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:27.540
They tested it in Scandinavia first.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.130
It was available in Sweden for a while.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.260
They also developed their own vegan cheese

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.210
because McDonald's couldn't
find a commercial vegan cheese

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.043
that they thought was good enough.

00:09:34.043 --> 00:09:36.480
Yeah, I believe it. Look at
this. This looks terrifying.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:37.313
I'll leave you to it, buddy.

00:09:37.313 --> 00:09:38.790
Thanks, bud. What he said.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:41.850
I think it was only available
in a few places in the US.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:43.890
Came and went.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.515
So, at least the US audience,

00:09:45.515 --> 00:09:47.232
not impressed with the McPlant.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.760
Yeah, that's not good.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:53.490
There is definitely some
plant-based meat that tastes good,

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.840
that tastes like meat.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:55.673
This ain't it.

00:09:55.673 --> 00:09:59.048
I want to take this moment
to try your UK Coca-Cola.

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:02.610
Man, the Coke here is way better.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:03.866
You guys make it with real sugar.

00:10:03.866 --> 00:10:06.514
F--- off with this!

00:10:06.514 --> 00:10:07.622
Does this ... ?

00:10:07.622 --> 00:10:09.270
And these are the dippers, right?

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:13.110
Who do you think you are, McDonald's?

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.150
Who do you think you are, doing this?

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:17.850
You just took the dippers and put them ...

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.200
Oh, God, gross!

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.283
What is this, like ... what is this?

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.167
Vegetables.

00:10:26.083 --> 00:10:27.840
Yo, this sucks ass, dude.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:30.000
Yeah, the vegetarian says he loves them.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.080
Put a asterisk next to that.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.210
Of all the things he
can eat at McDonald's,

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.320
there's two, right?

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.690
And this is one of them. So OK, great.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.415
I never want this.

00:10:39.448 --> 00:10:40.965
Moving on.

00:10:40.965 --> 00:10:42.090
Ah, Chicken Selects.

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:44.580
This is closer to what our McChicken

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.005
and our nuggets taste like.

00:10:48.607 --> 00:10:49.650
Oh, yeah.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.690
Damn, wish we had this in America.

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:53.760
The sour cream and chive
dip is really good.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.530
Here are all the
exclusive wraps and salads

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:58.140
that you can find in the US
that you won't find in the UK.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.180
That's not a mistake. There
are just none of them.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:01.467
It's not even that there's no exclusives.

00:11:01.467 --> 00:11:03.720
There's just no wraps
or salads, full stop,

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.460
on a US McDonald's menu.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:08.040
Joe: USA!

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.230
I can't exactly say that
the UK salads are good

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.090
at McDonald's, but at least
we have them, you know?

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:14.700
You have an option if you
somehow are trying to eat healthy

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.560
but have ended up in a McDonald's anyway.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:18.640
Whereas in America the closest
thing you have to a salad

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:20.837
is this bag of apple slices.

00:11:20.837 --> 00:11:24.180
Oh, my God. I hate wraps.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:27.990
This is a really smart way
of presenting this. A pita.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.203
Isn't that a pita?

00:11:29.203 --> 00:11:31.134
Harry: Tortilla, isn't it?

00:11:31.134 --> 00:11:33.308
Oh, yeah. I guess it's
closer to a tortilla.

00:11:33.308 --> 00:11:35.863
Leon: Also, the way you say it.

00:11:35.863 --> 00:11:36.817
Joe: "Peed-a."
Leon: Yeah.

00:11:36.817 --> 00:11:37.650
How do you say it?

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:38.483
Leon: "Pit-ta."

00:11:38.483 --> 00:11:41.121
No, that's wrong. It's
with an I. "Peed-a."

00:11:41.121 --> 00:11:42.060
Charlie: I would say "pit-ta."

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.244
Well, you'd be wrong.

00:11:48.406 --> 00:11:49.778
Ugh, what kind of dressing is this?

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.270
Well, it says garlic, but
it's not very garlicky.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:58.260
OK, so then we have the
grilled version of this. Yeah.

00:11:58.260 --> 00:11:59.843
No, no, no, no, no.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:05.940
What flavor could this possibly have?

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:07.981
Oh, come on.

00:12:07.981 --> 00:12:09.353
Charlie: I thought that
was a bit of bread!

00:12:09.353 --> 00:12:10.920
No.

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:14.220
Oh, man. That has no flavor.

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:17.520
Yeah, you can get a grilled-
or crispy-chicken salad,

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:18.550
but we didn't get them

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:21.780
because I didn't fly across
the planet to eat a salad.

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.720
Hey, this is fun. Nacho cheese wedges.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.360
Well, we're much further from Mexico,

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:29.793
so how good could the
nacho cheese actually be?

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:32.850
Not bad.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.090
It's certainly the most
flavorful thing I've eaten today.

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:37.590
Now it's time for the
exclusive condiments,

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:38.966
and you know what that means.

00:12:38.966 --> 00:12:42.003
S-s-s-s-s-s-sauce talk.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.758
The very first sauce
talk, "Foreign Exchange."

00:12:46.758 --> 00:12:48.570
Sauce talk.

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:51.020
We're going to start with
this one, spicy Buffalo.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.888
Yeah, so I think that's
the same one that they put

00:12:53.888 --> 00:12:55.630
on the spicy McCrispy.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:57.938
It's pretty good. It's basically
like if you take a mayo

00:12:57.938 --> 00:12:59.310
and just pour some Frank's RedHot in it.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:01.020
Let's try the honey mustard out.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:02.973
I personally love a honey mustard.

00:13:03.995 --> 00:13:05.880
You certainly get the
honey. It's pretty good.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:09.390
I think the balance of that
is more on the honey side,

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.820
and it needs to swing slightly
more to the mustard side.

00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:13.470
Now, this one I'm excited for.

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:17.194
It's ranch. We call it
"rahnch," not ranch.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.670
Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:23.940
Yeah, it's got a sort of herby tang to it.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:24.990
Then we've got a couple of condiments

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.653
which are technically breakfast items

00:13:26.653 --> 00:13:28.350
but we're going to count
under sauce talk anyway.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:31.320
We'll start with the mild picante salsa.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:33.030
I think this is supposed to be paired

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:36.480
with the breakfast burrito,
which we will get onto later.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:37.852
But I'm going to try it with a nugget.

00:13:37.852 --> 00:13:39.102
Joe: Oh, Jesus.

00:13:40.383 --> 00:13:42.058
OK, that's enough.

00:13:42.058 --> 00:13:42.891
Just do it.

00:13:44.793 --> 00:13:46.290
Does what it says on the tin.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:48.840
That's just a mild salsa, really.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:50.100
Also on the breakfast-condiments list,

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.260
we have hotcake syrup.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.090
I guess, like, maybe
legally they're not allowed

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:57.300
to call it maple syrup, so hotcake syrup.

00:13:57.300 --> 00:14:00.330
I mean, people eat pancakes
with bacon and maple syrup,

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:03.540
so why can't chicken nuggets
and maple syrup go together?

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:06.239
OK, I thought I'd invented
something special there,

00:14:06.239 --> 00:14:09.090
but nope, turns out I cannot claim

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:10.830
that combination as my own.

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:12.510
It's butter.

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:13.667
They have butter on the menu.

00:14:13.667 --> 00:14:17.370
I think, again, designed to
be used with the hotcakes.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:20.880
The final condiment
option is some grape jam.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.655
I will say, we don't tend to have many

00:14:22.655 --> 00:14:25.122
grape-flavored products in
the UK for whatever reason.

00:14:28.841 --> 00:14:30.938
Mm.
Joe: Yeah?

00:14:30.938 --> 00:14:32.580
It's pretty tasty.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:33.960
Maybe not in combination with the chicken,

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.520
but the grape jam is quite nice.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.470
Already, your ketchup, it's bizarre.

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:41.250
It makes sense why this would be ketchup,

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:42.930
considering what ketchup is.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:45.390
But American ketchup is way sweeter.

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:46.620
I don't know if that's a
good thing or a bad thing,

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.690
but I'm eating that, and I'm like,

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:49.710
if that was on a plate,

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:51.310
I was eating somewhere
that that was on a plate

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:52.651
and I was dipping into it,

00:14:52.651 --> 00:14:54.210
I'd be like, "Oh, what sauce is this?"

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:55.440
Because I wouldn't think that's ketchup.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:57.270
Like, "Oh, it's this fun
tomato sauce you got."

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:58.811
I wouldn't go, "Oh, ketchup."

00:14:58.811 --> 00:15:00.327
Yeah, it's that different.

00:15:00.327 --> 00:15:03.170
OK, the barbecue sauce, from
the country with no barbecue.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.800
Let's see what you guys
think barbecue is. Nope.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.480
I don't know what this is supposed to be.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.580
Sweet chili dip. Here we go.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:13.396
Better. Just OK.

00:15:13.396 --> 00:15:15.778
McDonald's barbecue sauce is its own

00:15:15.778 --> 00:15:18.780
special brand of barbecue sauce.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:20.831
Yeah, this is pretty close to it, but

00:15:20.831 --> 00:15:23.865
this one's a little more mustardy.

00:15:23.865 --> 00:15:26.190
So, OK. Yeah, it's not bad.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:29.190
All right, sweet and sour.
Ooh, that's really good.

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:33.810
Oh, hell yeah, dude. Sweet
curry. Been waiting for this.

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:34.770
That's really good!

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:35.818
We don't have any exclusive options

00:15:35.818 --> 00:15:37.440
when it comes to the
food inside a Happy Meal,

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:38.760
but I did want to get one and just kind of

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:41.730
see what the vibe was, see
what the toy is, crucially.

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:43.777
So, at the time of recording this,

00:15:43.777 --> 00:15:45.540
"The Little Mermaid"
hit theaters recently,

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.510
so they seem to be doing a
collab with "The Little Mermaid."

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.700
Does that mean I'm going to
get a "Little Mermaid" toy?

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:51.817
Let's find out.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:56.490
So, we get — oh, these fries are so cute.

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:59.898
So, this is a UK large. [Joe laughing]

00:15:59.898 --> 00:16:01.414
This is what I'm used to.

00:16:01.414 --> 00:16:04.382
I will say, in the UK, the
fries come in a paper bag

00:16:04.382 --> 00:16:05.920
rather than one of these

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.670
simply adorable little cartons,

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:10.710
which, honestly, huge fan of.

00:16:10.710 --> 00:16:12.750
I went for the McNuggets,

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:15.510
which tend to come in a box of four.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:17.310
Ah, there you go. You get
the apple slices within that.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:19.501
This is the American salad.

00:16:19.501 --> 00:16:21.810
And, of course, we get a toy.

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:24.090
Oh, it's King Triton! Let's go!

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:27.480
"Place your toy on a phone
or tablet for more fun,"

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:29.610
which I do think we have
to try and do real quick.

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:30.840
OK, try again. OK, put it down.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.348
Put my phone on the desk.

00:16:32.348 --> 00:16:33.933
You guys are getting this, right?

00:16:33.933 --> 00:16:35.460
Getting all of this? This is crucial.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:38.402
Place your toy on there. Pick a thing.

00:16:38.402 --> 00:16:39.450
I'll just go there.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:40.500
OK. Play the game.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.076
"Turn your sound on."

00:16:42.076 --> 00:16:46.050
[water swooshing]

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:48.960
I'm going to be honest. This is a miss.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.573
Some kind of pattern? "Learn pattern."

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.396
That one, that one.

00:16:54.396 --> 00:16:56.031
[water swooshing]

00:16:56.031 --> 00:16:57.660
Did it. I win.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.000
DC Happy Meal.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.300
I've been told that it's —
one second. We got the toy.

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:07.170
Oh, Poison Ivy. Fast-food
fish is way more popular here.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:11.070
You guys love your fast fish. I do not.

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:12.311
It smells fishy.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:17.873
For the first time,

00:17:17.873 --> 00:17:20.370
your food being flavorless
is a good thing.

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:21.630
Fries. Yeah, actually,

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:23.820
I would say this is also our kids size.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:25.160
Let's take a look at the Poison Ivy toy.

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:27.376
What the hell? What is — OK.

00:17:27.376 --> 00:17:28.784
Oh, there's something inside.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:33.053
Ah, stickers, a game.

00:17:33.053 --> 00:17:35.161
All right. Fun for kids.

00:17:35.161 --> 00:17:37.140
Now we're on to some
McCafé and dessert options.

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:38.880
Unfortunately, I couldn't
get a few of these,

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:40.620
but here are the ones that
I was able to find today.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:42.322
We'll start with a good
old-fashioned American

00:17:42.322 --> 00:17:44.163
chocolate chip cookie.
This looks pretty good.

00:17:44.163 --> 00:17:45.572
We're kind of bad at cookies in the UK.

00:17:45.572 --> 00:17:47.615
I don't know what it
is, but they tend to be

00:17:47.615 --> 00:17:51.003
very dry and crumbly
rather than soft and chewy.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:53.543
That's not bad.

00:17:53.543 --> 00:17:55.260
What's more American than apple pie?

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:58.380
I'll tell you what, an
apple pie from McDonald's.

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:01.290
This is the American McDonald's apple pie.

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:04.080
In the UK, a McDonald's apple
pie is actually deep-fried.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:05.190
It just looks very different.

00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:06.690
This is a baked apple pie,

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:08.280
so you get more of a lattice going on.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:09.897
You see the filling there, but it's baked,

00:18:09.897 --> 00:18:12.635
so I guess they don't need
to seal it on every side

00:18:12.635 --> 00:18:13.620
because it's not going in a fryer.

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:15.270
It's not all going to
spill out into the oil.

00:18:15.270 --> 00:18:16.945
I don't know if it's
going to hold up or not.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:21.030
I think the UK might be
doing better apple pies

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:23.520
than the US is, at least
when it comes to McDonald's.

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:25.290
The pastry's fine.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:26.820
The filling tastes pretty much identical

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:29.220
to the filling of a UK apple pie.

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:30.961
But yeah, like, the baked pastry

00:18:30.961 --> 00:18:32.550
is just not the same as fried pastry.

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.500
And then there's actually
another pie option

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.420
on the menu right now at a US McDonald's.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:38.343
This one is a strawberry cream pie.

00:18:39.245 --> 00:18:40.380
That's pretty good.

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:42.060
As I said, there were
some desserts and pastries

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:44.490
that we weren't able to
get today. Here they are.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:47.490
In the UK, you can also
get exclusive McFlurries.

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.020
Could not get them because,
you're not going to believe it,

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:51.330
but the ice cream machines
are also broken in the UK.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:53.757
You can get yourself a Maltesers McFlurry

00:18:53.757 --> 00:18:55.470
and a Smarties McFlurry.

00:18:55.470 --> 00:18:59.070
OK, we got the McCafé snacks.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.390
First up, oh, a doughnut.

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:01.448
Hey, who doesn't like a doughnut?

00:19:01.448 --> 00:19:03.490
Ooh, yo!

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:05.940
This one is covered in
sugar. Look at that.

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:09.630
Muffin. Berry. Berry muffin.

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:11.313
A millionaire's doughnut, huh?

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:15.540
Ooh, with the cream inside?

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:16.590
It is pretty decadent.

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:17.948
I don't know if I feel like a millionaire.

00:19:17.948 --> 00:19:19.050
I don't think millionaires
are eating those,

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:20.460
I'm going to be honest with you.

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:22.620
Oh, hell yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:23.700
Yep. That's a good cookie.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:24.870
Let's talk about the drinks.

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:26.790
First of all, there are
some hot and cold coffees

00:19:26.790 --> 00:19:28.320
which are available in both countries.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:30.288
It does seem like the US
actually has a bigger range

00:19:30.288 --> 00:19:32.940
of coffees, particularly when
it comes to the iced versions,

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:34.972
while in the UK we're limited
to a couple of basic ones

00:19:34.972 --> 00:19:37.020
like an iced latte. Over
here you can get all sorts.

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:39.810
You can get things like
your iced caramel mocha,

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:43.740
your frappa mochaccino,
Dunkin' thingymajiggy.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:44.610
You know the ones.

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:46.320
There are some interesting
non-coffee drinks though

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:47.910
that I do want to try and talk about now.

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:49.230
We're going to start with
this one down the end,

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:51.046
which I believe is Hawaiian Punch.

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:54.516
Not common in the UK at all.

00:19:57.615 --> 00:19:58.810
Joe: [laughs] Yep.

00:19:58.810 --> 00:20:00.540
OK.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:01.470
If this is the first one,

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.510
I think I have a bit
of a storm coming here.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:05.550
It's pretty good, but, wow, is that sweet.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:08.460
This one is an American-style lemonade.

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:09.840
As I've said before in the show,

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:11.880
lemonade in the UK is like Sprite.

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:14.790
It's, like, a clear,
carbonated lemony beverage,

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:17.490
whereas this looks like
a good old-fashioned

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:19.470
American lemonade.

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:21.295
It's not bad. It's weird to me

00:20:21.295 --> 00:20:22.890
that lemonade isn't carbonated,

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:25.090
but that's pretty good. That's
actually fairly refreshing,

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:27.240
unlike maybe the Hawaiian Punch was.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:30.600
Also, happy birthday, Grimace,
while we're on the subject.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:32.670
They did have a special Grimace shake,

00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:34.958
but the ice cream machine was broken

00:20:34.958 --> 00:20:37.020
at the McDonald's that
we went to, of course,

00:20:37.020 --> 00:20:38.280
so I haven't been able
to get the Grimace shake,

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:39.113
which I'm really sad about.

00:20:39.113 --> 00:20:41.220
Here's what it's supposed to look like.

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:43.393
They do not have a good
old-fashioned cup of tea

00:20:43.393 --> 00:20:45.270
on the menu at an American McDonald's.

00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:47.370
What they do have is sweet tea.

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:48.930
I felt like I had to try it as a Brit.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:51.602
You know, I have to give my
thoughts on everyone's teas.

00:20:52.452 --> 00:20:55.440
Aah.
Joe: [laughs] No!

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:58.170
They weren't kidding when
they called it sweet tea.

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:01.560
So, this was supposed to be a
blue-raspberry frozen Fanta,

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.300
and this was supposed to be a frozen Coke.

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:06.600
However, now it is just a
melted blue-raspberry Fanta

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:09.033
and a melted Coke,
otherwise known as Coke.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.783
Ooh. That's pretty good.

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:15.990
Yeah, just tastes like Coke.

00:21:15.990 --> 00:21:19.110
It does somehow, like, still
has a bit of fizz to it,

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:20.670
and the same with the Fanta, actually.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.850
I do think I would like
these if they were frozen.

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:25.680
I think on a really hot day, for example,

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.510
carrying a frozen Coke
around sounds delightful.

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:31.320
So, yeah, would quite like
those on the UK menu, maybe.

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:35.130
Then we have a, what I
believe to be, Hi-C drink,

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:37.830
Hi-C Orange Lavaburst.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:41.220
Yeah, so this isn't carbonated,
and it's not fruit juice.

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:43.140
It's somewhere in the middle.

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:46.560
I'd put it reasonably close to an Oasis

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:47.820
that we can get in the UK,

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:50.620
which is also a sort of
non-carbonated fruity beverage.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:51.503
I don't love it.

00:21:51.503 --> 00:21:54.990
Last but by no means least,
we have milk on the menu.

00:21:54.990 --> 00:21:56.730
I think this is kind of aimed at kids.

00:21:56.730 --> 00:22:01.020
I never want to meet a
person who is a grown adult

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:03.330
and goes to McDonald's and
orders milk with their meal.

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:04.770
These are all the exclusive
drinks we got today.

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:06.660
There are some other
ones, and here they are.

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:09.090
All right, the McCafé exclusives.

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:11.100
They didn't label any of
them, so I'll just guess.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:12.743
That's definitely hot
chocolate, but let's see,

00:22:12.743 --> 00:22:14.790
how does it compare to the deluxe?

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:15.873
Mm-mm.

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:18.090
Oh, this is that butter
thing. That's terrible.

00:22:18.090 --> 00:22:20.007
We'll get back to that. Let me
find the other hot chocolate.

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:22.510
That's a hot chocolate.

00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:25.020
I can't tell the difference.

00:22:25.020 --> 00:22:27.630
I don't know which one's
deluxe. Would deluxe be size?

00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:30.390
Wait, this one has that
buttery oil floating in it.

00:22:30.390 --> 00:22:33.453
And this, I know what this is.

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:35.752
Tea!

00:22:38.373 --> 00:22:40.980
I don't get it. I don't
get why this is so popular.

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:42.450
The McCafé food's pretty good. I like it.

00:22:42.450 --> 00:22:45.180
You got a good selection
here. The drinks, not so much.

00:22:45.180 --> 00:22:47.288
I like banana, I like
banana-flavored stuff,

00:22:47.288 --> 00:22:50.140
and we don't nearly have as
much in the United States.

00:22:50.140 --> 00:22:54.502
This tastes exactly like a
banana Laffy Taffy. It's great.

00:22:54.502 --> 00:22:56.250
What's Oasis?

00:22:56.250 --> 00:22:57.540
Yeah, no, thanks.

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:00.349
I mean, it's sweet, but
it reminds me of Gatorade.

00:23:00.349 --> 00:23:01.680
Orange juice. I know what
orange juice tastes like.

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:05.340
What is this? Robinsons Fruit Shoot.

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:07.440
Why is it a Fruit Shoot?
What's the shooting part?

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:08.550
Leon: It's for kids, really.

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:09.958
Oh, so it's just, like,
shoot it in my mouth,

00:23:09.958 --> 00:23:11.408
like, "aah"? That what it's for?

00:23:11.408 --> 00:23:13.676
Leon: I think it's called that
because kids are more likely

00:23:13.676 --> 00:23:15.060
to be like, "Yeah, give me a Fruit Shoot."

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:16.018
Than what?

00:23:16.018 --> 00:23:17.790
Leon: Than, like, "Give me a Coke."

00:23:17.790 --> 00:23:20.356
I would like to know why
this is called Fruit Shoot.

00:23:20.356 --> 00:23:22.061
OK, so I think it's called,
I haven't looked it up,

00:23:22.061 --> 00:23:23.289
I think it's called Fruit
Shoot because it wants you

00:23:23.289 --> 00:23:25.528
to squeeze, like, shoot it
in your mouth, like, "blah!"

00:23:26.850 --> 00:23:28.560
And Leon thinks it's because

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:30.810
it sounds better than saying Coke.

00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:32.250
Now we're going to talk
about the most important meal

00:23:32.250 --> 00:23:33.330
of the day, breakfast.

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:35.790
We'll start with this one,
the steak and egg McMuffin.

00:23:35.790 --> 00:23:39.480
That doesn't really look,
taste, or feel like a steak.

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:42.540
Now, next up, America has some
breakfast biscuit options.

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:43.620
So, from what I've seen,

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:45.990
a biscuit looks very much like a scone,

00:23:45.990 --> 00:23:48.390
which is obviously a classic British dish.

00:23:48.390 --> 00:23:51.270
Now, the fact that they would
be putting breakfast food,

00:23:51.270 --> 00:23:53.100
like bacon, eggs, sausages,

00:23:53.100 --> 00:23:56.400
into what is effectively
a scone is weird to me

00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:58.260
and I think will be weird
to a lot of Brits as well.

00:23:58.260 --> 00:24:00.780
So, this is just a
classic sausage biscuit.

00:24:00.780 --> 00:24:03.420
It does look pretty like a scone.

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.820
It's maybe a bit more,
like, smooth on the outside

00:24:05.820 --> 00:24:06.995
than I'm expecting from a scone.

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:10.320
So dry.

00:24:10.320 --> 00:24:11.520
Joe: Told you.
Harry: Oh, my God.

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:12.493
Hey, Joe from "Food Wars" here.

00:24:12.493 --> 00:24:14.340
I just wanted to say, that's not a scone.

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:15.420
It's a different biscuit.

00:24:15.420 --> 00:24:16.950
I don't know what he's talking about.

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:18.300
He'll be chewing on that
for the next four minutes,

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:19.440
but it's different.

00:24:19.440 --> 00:24:20.550
He's right. It's different.

00:24:20.550 --> 00:24:22.530
It's not a scone. It's somehow worse.

00:24:22.530 --> 00:24:23.610
Yeah, apparently I chose badly

00:24:23.610 --> 00:24:24.900
with the sausage being my first one,

00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:26.670
because that was dry as a desert.

00:24:26.670 --> 00:24:29.310
So let's have a quick bite
of a bacon, egg, and cheese,

00:24:29.310 --> 00:24:32.463
which is a classic American-slash-New
York breakfast combo.

00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:34.920
It's still pretty dry, but the addition

00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:36.330
of the other stuff definitely helps.

00:24:36.330 --> 00:24:38.430
What are the takeaways there?

00:24:38.430 --> 00:24:41.618
Scones and biscuits are
different, not the same.

00:24:41.618 --> 00:24:44.070
A scone is a little bit more crumbly,

00:24:44.070 --> 00:24:46.230
generally slightly sweeter.

00:24:46.230 --> 00:24:50.340
These are not sweet.
Slightly more bready texture.

00:24:50.340 --> 00:24:53.370
I'm still not convinced by
the notion of them as, like,

00:24:53.370 --> 00:24:54.810
the foundation of a breakfast sandwich,

00:24:54.810 --> 00:24:56.850
just mostly because of how dry they are.

00:24:56.850 --> 00:24:59.280
But, hey, who am I to
judge American culture?

00:24:59.280 --> 00:25:00.210
Now, these I'm excited for.

00:25:00.210 --> 00:25:01.680
I've heard very good things
about these from Joe.

00:25:01.680 --> 00:25:03.840
These are McDonald's McGriddles.

00:25:03.840 --> 00:25:06.300
If I remember correctly
from watching Joe eat these,

00:25:06.300 --> 00:25:11.078
they've got pancakes that
they sort of inject with syrup

00:25:11.078 --> 00:25:13.845
and then use those as the
buns for a breakfast sandwich,

00:25:13.845 --> 00:25:15.690
which sounds pretty excellent.

00:25:15.690 --> 00:25:18.390
I'll try the bacon, egg, and
cheese. See how we get on.

00:25:19.980 --> 00:25:21.870
Still slightly dry, but way less dry

00:25:21.870 --> 00:25:23.550
than the biscuit, and very tasty.

00:25:23.550 --> 00:25:24.983
I'm going to go even more syrup,

00:25:24.983 --> 00:25:27.148
because what's better
than adding more syrup

00:25:27.148 --> 00:25:30.167
to something which is
already full of syrup?

00:25:30.167 --> 00:25:35.010
McGriddles, yes. Biscuits, not so sure.

00:25:35.010 --> 00:25:36.720
So, this was the bacon,
egg, and cheese McGriddle.

00:25:36.720 --> 00:25:38.760
You can also get McGriddles with sausage,

00:25:38.760 --> 00:25:41.310
sausage and egg and cheese, or the steak,

00:25:41.310 --> 00:25:42.690
which I will not be trying.

00:25:42.690 --> 00:25:44.015
The next exclusive breakfast item

00:25:44.015 --> 00:25:47.280
is the bacon, egg, and
cheese breakfast bagel.

00:25:47.280 --> 00:25:50.490
We used to have bagels on the
menu at the UK McDonald's,

00:25:50.490 --> 00:25:51.960
and they were wonderful.

00:25:51.960 --> 00:25:53.340
Part of the breakfast menu,

00:25:53.340 --> 00:25:56.607
toasted bagels with your choice
of toppings and fillings,

00:25:56.607 --> 00:25:57.540
really good.

00:25:57.540 --> 00:25:59.790
Pandemic hit, they cut them from the menu,

00:25:59.790 --> 00:26:01.180
and they've not returned.

00:26:01.180 --> 00:26:03.247
And personally, I'm furious about that.

00:26:06.060 --> 00:26:08.280
Yeah. I've missed you so much, bagel.

00:26:08.280 --> 00:26:10.440
Next up, we have a sausage burrito.

00:26:10.440 --> 00:26:13.200
Breakfast burrito is really
not a thing in the UK.

00:26:13.200 --> 00:26:15.810
We're just generally bad at Mexican food.

00:26:15.810 --> 00:26:17.310
This is obviously designed to be enjoyed

00:26:17.310 --> 00:26:18.780
with the mild salsa.

00:26:18.780 --> 00:26:19.950
It's actually pretty good.

00:26:19.950 --> 00:26:21.720
And then lastly on the
breakfast menu, we have these,

00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:23.130
the Big Breakfasts.

00:26:23.130 --> 00:26:28.123
The standard Big Breakfast
is a slab of scrambled egg,

00:26:28.123 --> 00:26:29.820
a sausage patty, and a biscuit.

00:26:29.820 --> 00:26:32.250
And this is the Big
Breakfast with hotcakes,

00:26:32.250 --> 00:26:34.500
which is the egg, biscuit, and sausage

00:26:34.500 --> 00:26:36.690
but then also comes with two pancakes.

00:26:36.690 --> 00:26:38.670
Both of these come with dips,
including a little thing

00:26:38.670 --> 00:26:41.700
of whipped butter and, of
course, the hotcake syrup.

00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:42.990
So, I wasn't sure what the difference was

00:26:42.990 --> 00:26:45.270
between pancakes and hotcakes.

00:26:45.270 --> 00:26:47.897
Joe's just done a quick
Google, and apparently,

00:26:47.897 --> 00:26:51.090
hotcakes tend to be a bit
thicker and denser than pancakes.

00:26:51.090 --> 00:26:53.250
I mean, to me, that just
tastes like a pancake.

00:26:53.250 --> 00:26:55.830
I'm thinking maybe they've
just called them hotcakes

00:26:55.830 --> 00:26:57.210
to make them sound more
fancy or different,

00:26:57.210 --> 00:26:59.040
but, yeah, not bad.

00:26:59.040 --> 00:27:02.400
And, of course, McDonald's
UK, I gotta try the breakfast.

00:27:02.400 --> 00:27:06.270
All right, first up,
the mini potato waffles,

00:27:06.270 --> 00:27:07.740
hash browns that are shaped like a waffle.

00:27:07.740 --> 00:27:09.523
I don't know why this specific shape.

00:27:11.970 --> 00:27:13.020
Yeah, dude.

00:27:13.020 --> 00:27:14.970
For some reason, it tastes
a lot better in waffle form.

00:27:14.970 --> 00:27:16.753
I don't know why that is.
These are really good.

00:27:16.753 --> 00:27:19.140
What do we got here? Breakfast sandwich.

00:27:19.140 --> 00:27:23.026
This is the bacon roll with brown sauce.

00:27:23.026 --> 00:27:25.503
It's like a hamburger bun! Look at this.

00:27:26.340 --> 00:27:27.990
There's your brown sauce right there.

00:27:27.990 --> 00:27:30.256
Hm. Eh.

00:27:30.256 --> 00:27:33.290
It's just OK. Nothing special. It's bland.

00:27:34.570 --> 00:27:36.270
I'm starting to think that you in the UK,

00:27:36.270 --> 00:27:38.593
you guys don't like, your
stuff isn't as, like,

00:27:38.593 --> 00:27:41.250
intense as ours in America is.

00:27:41.250 --> 00:27:44.893
Like, this wouldn't fly
in the US because it's not

00:27:44.893 --> 00:27:47.790
dripping with cheese and
doesn't have an egg in it

00:27:47.790 --> 00:27:49.773
and the buns aren't, like, über-buttery.

00:27:50.700 --> 00:27:52.170
It's just too plain. It's too boring.

00:27:52.170 --> 00:27:53.754
This is the same thing with just ketchup.

00:27:56.310 --> 00:27:57.985
Aw.

00:27:57.985 --> 00:28:00.660
Now we're getting more in my speed.

00:28:00.660 --> 00:28:03.120
This one has cheese and
bacon in it. Oh, yeah.

00:28:03.120 --> 00:28:04.650
Is that sausage?

00:28:04.650 --> 00:28:05.833
Yeah, this looks more like something

00:28:05.833 --> 00:28:07.974
that you'd get in the US.

00:28:07.974 --> 00:28:11.271
Yeah. Cheesy flatbread, oh, God.

00:28:13.290 --> 00:28:16.680
Cheesy — oh, come on, guys.
Yeah, see, this is the bacon.

00:28:16.680 --> 00:28:18.060
This is more like the bacon we're used to.

00:28:18.060 --> 00:28:19.830
Charlie: So, that's streaky bacon.

00:28:19.830 --> 00:28:21.902
Streaky bacon? So, this is bacon,

00:28:21.902 --> 00:28:25.141
and the other thing was
Canadian bacon in the US.

00:28:25.141 --> 00:28:28.350
I don't know why. Or ham,
I'm going to call it.

00:28:28.350 --> 00:28:30.049
I mean, this just looks like,

00:28:30.049 --> 00:28:31.499
I mean, this looks like whatever.

00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:36.354
Yeah, this sucks. And that's why it sucks.

00:28:36.354 --> 00:28:38.820
It's like, the flatbread is too strong.

00:28:38.820 --> 00:28:40.410
I can barely taste the streaky bacon,

00:28:40.410 --> 00:28:41.970
which is what I came here for, so.

00:28:41.970 --> 00:28:44.550
Double sausage. OK, so with this,

00:28:44.550 --> 00:28:46.500
you guys just went double meat on both.

00:28:49.007 --> 00:28:51.408
Oh, man! Yo!

00:28:51.408 --> 00:28:54.900
Look how much sausage is
in here. Look at that!

00:28:54.900 --> 00:28:59.430
Hell yeah. Now we're talking, UK. See?

00:28:59.430 --> 00:29:01.193
Although, nothing in between

00:29:01.193 --> 00:29:02.960
the two sausage patties is, like,

00:29:04.110 --> 00:29:05.940
it's gotta go cheese, meat, cheese, meat.

00:29:05.940 --> 00:29:08.970
You can't just do meat. This doesn't work.

00:29:08.970 --> 00:29:11.717
And possibly a sauce. No
sauce is weird for this one.

00:29:11.717 --> 00:29:13.440
Your sausage is weird.

00:29:13.440 --> 00:29:15.990
I would say ours is spicier. Not heat,

00:29:15.990 --> 00:29:18.780
but the flavor of the
sausage is more pronounced

00:29:18.780 --> 00:29:20.220
in the US one compared to this.

00:29:20.220 --> 00:29:22.570
So, I know in the US, our
sausage is made up of,

00:29:23.670 --> 00:29:26.470
and from what I understand,
the UK sausage is made up of.

00:29:28.020 --> 00:29:30.368
And that was all done in post.
I have no idea what it says.

00:29:30.368 --> 00:29:31.943
Like, here's the thing.

00:29:31.943 --> 00:29:34.770
I like the double, but needs more cheese,

00:29:34.770 --> 00:29:36.720
needs to be drowning
in some sort of sauce.

00:29:36.720 --> 00:29:40.273
But this one I'm assuming
then is double bacon.

00:29:42.740 --> 00:29:44.317
No, this is not double bacon.

00:29:44.317 --> 00:29:48.870
Wait, one, two pieces
of bacon's double bacon?

00:29:48.870 --> 00:29:51.570
This is double for you guys? For real?

00:29:51.570 --> 00:29:53.580
Yo, you're getting ripped off, guys.

00:29:53.580 --> 00:29:55.320
Excuse me, you've made a mistake.

00:29:55.320 --> 00:29:57.975
You come back in like, come
storming in and cut in the line,

00:29:57.975 --> 00:29:59.460
be like, "Ah, you made a mistake on mine.

00:29:59.460 --> 00:30:01.170
There's only one slice of bacon on this."

00:30:01.170 --> 00:30:03.993
So, all right. Let's try
with this double bacon.

00:30:05.070 --> 00:30:06.487
I mean, it's ham.

00:30:08.670 --> 00:30:12.480
Yeah, that's standard. That's not double.

00:30:12.480 --> 00:30:13.650
This is smart that they did the jam.

00:30:13.650 --> 00:30:16.710
I don't know in the US they
have the squirtable one.

00:30:16.710 --> 00:30:17.826
I mean, do I need to, like,

00:30:17.826 --> 00:30:20.130
I mean, I know what a
muffin and jam taste like.

00:30:20.130 --> 00:30:21.197
I'm not like ...

00:30:21.197 --> 00:30:23.880
Harry: Have you had a
British muffin and jam?

00:30:23.880 --> 00:30:24.713
If I eat this,

00:30:24.713 --> 00:30:27.660
will I still have had a
British muffin and jam?

00:30:27.660 --> 00:30:29.368
I think after this, I
still will have no idea

00:30:29.368 --> 00:30:31.193
what a British muffin and jam taste like.

00:30:31.193 --> 00:30:32.026
All right, all right, all right.

00:30:32.026 --> 00:30:33.518
All right, everyone relax.

00:30:35.880 --> 00:30:37.590
Oh, yeah, that is really good.

00:30:37.590 --> 00:30:39.600
This tastes way better
than the crap that we have.

00:30:39.600 --> 00:30:40.758
Like, way better!

00:30:40.758 --> 00:30:42.450
So, I have just been
informed that in England,

00:30:42.450 --> 00:30:44.640
these are just called
muffins, not English muffins.

00:30:44.640 --> 00:30:48.150
Porridge. I'm from the US.

00:30:48.150 --> 00:30:51.240
I don't know what porridge
is. I'm assuming it's oatmeal?

00:30:51.240 --> 00:30:53.070
So, from what I can tell,

00:30:53.070 --> 00:30:54.480
you can get porridge four different ways.

00:30:54.480 --> 00:30:56.910
One with golden syrup,
looks a lot like honey;

00:30:56.910 --> 00:31:00.120
one with strawberry jam,
straight from France;

00:31:00.120 --> 00:31:03.030
one with sugar, which
they did not include;

00:31:03.030 --> 00:31:04.380
and then one plain.

00:31:04.380 --> 00:31:08.700
So, first I'm just going
straight porridge, no chaser.

00:31:08.700 --> 00:31:11.010
Yeah, that has no flavor to it.

00:31:11.010 --> 00:31:12.210
Leon: Have some golden syrup on the side.

00:31:12.210 --> 00:31:13.590
Yeah, all right.

00:31:13.590 --> 00:31:16.770
So, I've been informed that
golden syrup is good stuff.

00:31:16.770 --> 00:31:18.417
I don't know what's the
difference between golden syrup

00:31:18.417 --> 00:31:21.360
and I guess whatever other syrups.

00:31:21.360 --> 00:31:22.260
You're right, it's like,

00:31:22.260 --> 00:31:25.860
it's not quite maple syrup,
but it's pretty close.

00:31:25.860 --> 00:31:27.344
Makes it much better, obviously.

00:31:29.820 --> 00:31:32.474
Joe: All right. Overall, Harry,
of the American exclusives,

00:31:32.474 --> 00:31:35.550
what were some of your likes
and some of your dislikes?

00:31:35.550 --> 00:31:37.474
Hm. Some of the things I liked,

00:31:37.474 --> 00:31:40.200
you guys have a much bigger
breakfast menu than we do.

00:31:40.200 --> 00:31:41.220
I did like the McGriddles.

00:31:41.220 --> 00:31:43.415
They did live up to Joe's
pretty high billing.

00:31:43.415 --> 00:31:44.250
Joe: Mm-hmm.

00:31:44.250 --> 00:31:46.890
I also think that your bacon
is much better than ours.

00:31:46.890 --> 00:31:49.365
So I think maybe the double
Quarter Pounder with bacon

00:31:49.365 --> 00:31:51.510
was a strong highlight there.

00:31:51.510 --> 00:31:54.420
Some dislikes, there's a few.

00:31:54.420 --> 00:31:56.820
I don't like the
biscuits. I'm sorry, guys.

00:31:56.820 --> 00:31:58.249
I think they are, like,

00:31:58.249 --> 00:32:00.300
for a British person,
too similar to a scone.

00:32:00.300 --> 00:32:02.040
So we can't really mentally differentiate

00:32:02.040 --> 00:32:05.007
between the two, and it's just quite dry.

00:32:05.007 --> 00:32:08.010
And also I think, like,
making your burgers deluxe

00:32:08.010 --> 00:32:10.555
by just adding loads of mayo, some tomato,

00:32:10.555 --> 00:32:12.690
and lettuce just is a bit underwhelming.

00:32:12.690 --> 00:32:14.250
Not really a deluxe vibe for me.

00:32:14.250 --> 00:32:16.650
Joe: So, if you could
bring one thing to the UK

00:32:16.650 --> 00:32:19.290
from the US, exclusive, what would it be?

00:32:19.290 --> 00:32:20.730
If I could take one of these exclusives

00:32:20.730 --> 00:32:23.398
that I've tried today back to
the UK with me for our menu,

00:32:23.398 --> 00:32:24.263
I think I'm going to have to pick

00:32:24.263 --> 00:32:25.800
the bacon, egg, and cheese McGriddle.

00:32:25.800 --> 00:32:26.850
I think it was really good.

00:32:26.850 --> 00:32:29.550
It's a bit of a twist on the
classic McMuffin formula.

00:32:29.550 --> 00:32:31.290
Feels a little bit more decadent, maybe,

00:32:31.290 --> 00:32:32.970
a little bit more sweet.

00:32:32.970 --> 00:32:34.560
And, yeah, just really good fun.

00:32:34.560 --> 00:32:36.720
I like the emphasis you guys
place on your breakfast menu.

00:32:36.720 --> 00:32:37.950
Joe: And what was the thing
you just hated the most,

00:32:37.950 --> 00:32:39.800
you're like, "Ugh, let
that stay in the US"?

00:32:40.806 --> 00:32:42.720
Well, the thing that I hated the most

00:32:42.720 --> 00:32:46.397
and would want to remove
from all possible menus,

00:32:46.397 --> 00:32:48.640
it's tricky. There are a couple.

00:32:49.890 --> 00:32:52.050
But I think it might have
to be the sausage biscuit.

00:32:52.050 --> 00:32:53.730
It was so dry.

00:32:53.730 --> 00:32:57.810
And the notion of a
biscuit-slash-scone breakfast sandwich

00:32:57.810 --> 00:32:59.820
to a British person is just too bizarre.

00:32:59.820 --> 00:33:03.120
I can't get my head around
it. And, yeah, not the best.

00:33:03.120 --> 00:33:04.740
Gotta say, I really disliked your bacon.

00:33:04.740 --> 00:33:06.480
Your bacon is weird.

00:33:06.480 --> 00:33:08.255
It ruined everything that it was on.

00:33:08.255 --> 00:33:11.760
I love bacon, but your bacon
is just, it is bizarre.

00:33:11.760 --> 00:33:13.350
The things I liked the most,

00:33:13.350 --> 00:33:15.360
I obviously like the curry dipping sauce.

00:33:15.360 --> 00:33:18.090
I like the banana milkshake,
separately, obviously.

00:33:18.090 --> 00:33:20.760
That triple chocolate
chip cookie was good.

00:33:20.760 --> 00:33:21.935
Harry: All right, Joe,
you gotta pick one thing

00:33:21.935 --> 00:33:23.735
to take back with you
to the US from our menu

00:33:23.735 --> 00:33:25.260
and you gotta pick one thing to remove

00:33:25.260 --> 00:33:26.769
from our menu forever.

00:33:26.769 --> 00:33:30.150
I'm taking back the curry dipping sauce.

00:33:30.150 --> 00:33:34.271
I've wanted to try that since
we shot the first episode.

00:33:36.090 --> 00:33:39.068
And then, take off your menu,

00:33:40.140 --> 00:33:42.330
I mean, those veggie
dippers were pretty dismal,

00:33:42.330 --> 00:33:46.320
but I don't want to leave
vegetarians out in the lurch.

00:33:46.320 --> 00:33:48.813
The thing that's, like,
haunting me the most

00:33:48.813 --> 00:33:51.450
was the grilled-chicken wrap.

00:33:51.450 --> 00:33:53.490
I don't even think it was
grilled. I think it was boiled.

00:33:53.490 --> 00:33:57.390
And I feel bad that that's
on your menu, and it's gross.

00:33:57.390 --> 00:34:00.810
And I will do the UK a favor:

00:34:00.810 --> 00:34:02.760
all grilled chicken off
the menu, McDonald's.

00:34:02.760 --> 00:34:03.593
You're welcome.

00:34:03.593 --> 00:34:06.810
All right.
[horn blaring]

00:34:06.810 --> 00:34:08.760
Rolling.

00:34:08.760 --> 00:34:10.863
I'm in New York, and I'm
outside a McDonald's.

00:34:10.863 --> 00:34:12.263
I'm going to go inside,
take a look around,

00:34:12.263 --> 00:34:15.163
and see how it compares to a
British McDonald's experience.

